  (text "panel label: AI5   (43, 61) mm" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 52 333 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "16373b25-fb41-5f1c-ae6c-15e9e77c3b34"))
  (text "panel label: AI6   (61, 61) mm" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 137 333 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1bff40a5-867c-5415-b836-f0eccb6d8f7b"))
  (text "panel label: AI7   (79, 61) mm" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 222 333 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d9c92f73-7430-5fe9-9fde-a57e68d7633f"))
  (text "panel label: AI8   (97, 61) mm" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 307 333 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "985e79b5-7848-5d7c-9e39-9a9e1f9e6fd2"))
  (text "panel label: SPARE   (115, 61) mm" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 392 333 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "60b19a58-6848-51be-87f1-5d383c6a4eb2"))
  (text "TTL1..8 out (5 V, 1 kohm series on the main board) + 2 x GND" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 40 355 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "017efdaa-d32b-5248-a702-a109712c8034"))
  (text "TX coil terminal, beside the TX SMA (kept: user 2026-09-16)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 128 355 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9c83e1e5-b934-533e-9a87-e36097d42369"))
  (text "Qwiic (vertical): sensor from the front; shell pads on GND" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 198 355 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "41c4dc06-ac01-55b7-ac80-f9127669b498"))
  (text "0.96 in I2C OLED (0x3C) on an 8.5 mm vertical socket: the module lies flat on four M2 stand-offs (holes in the footprint)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 278 355 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "98e34838-5258-5beb-9059-42306cefee4e"))
  (text "PWR is +3V3 from the link (1 kohm -> about 1 mA); WIFI / ACT come from GPIO43 / GPIO44 through JP1 / JP2 on the main board." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 355 340 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b149f037-b8f3-5e2c-a200-013ac12d6226"))
  (text "panel label: PWR" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 388 362 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b735c9c9-d333-53d4-877a-059946091ae0"))
  (text "panel label: WIFI" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 388 379.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ee2c59d3-2f72-58d6-ab46-29daff413ca9"))
  (text "panel label: ACT" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 388 397.56 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "4480b27a-63fd-54da-8c7d-370fb5fce90f"))
  (text "MOD1..8 come from the main board's TCA9535 expander at 3.3 V on J3 pins 19..33. ONE 74AHCT541 on +5V_RAW lifts them to 5 V TTL (AHCT thresholds accept 3.3 V); 47 ohm in series limits a shorted output and damps the ribbon cable." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 604 22 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a537ec42-860a-5072-bc08-8fae2bcc2245"))
  (text "Both output enables are tied to GND, so the buffer is always on: the module lines are held low by the expander's own power-up state, not by a 3-state." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 604 26 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "861c816f-af0c-5650-906f-dde466b8831e"))
  (text "J40 is a POLARISED shrouded 2x6 IDC box header (XFCN BH254V-12P): 1,2 = +5V_RAW   3..10 = MODOUT1..8   11,12 = GND. Module current comes from +5V_RAW through the link - budget it, the rail is fused at 1.5 A on the main board." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 604 30 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b7e47c64-de54-5573-970b-ae6de11bb578"))
  (text "R491..R498: 10 k pull-down on every module line (the expander boots with its ports as inputs). MOD8 = J3 pin 33 is a reserved spare with no main-board driver at all." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 604 34 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1a6492ad-776c-531f-98cc-a13b1112697f"))
  (text "100 nF at the 541's VCC pin" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 744 65 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "63eb98d3-629c-5273-a899-f84f713b2dbf"))
  (text "panel label: MODULE OUT 1..7  5 V TTL  (8 = spare)   relay / H-bridge modules" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 744 190 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a42cc75d-92f1-5335-9840-7bd0909c627c"))
  (text "Series 1N4148W (reverse blocking) -> 220 R -> Q1 pass transistor with Q2 sensing 0.65 V across Rs (100 R || 1 k = 91 R): LED current about 6.5-7 mA from 5 V to 24 V (the 6N137 needs 5-15 mA). At 24 V Q1 dissipates about 125 mW (MMBT5551 is rated 300 mW)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 604 218 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6651fe4d-9235-5673-8ad6-a58626385a66"))
  (text "6N137S: VCC and VE on +3V3, 1 k pull-up, output LOW when the input is driven (inverting), 75 ns, 5 kVrms isolation. OPTO_IN1/2 leave on J3 pins 35/37 and land on the ESP32's GPIO16/17 through the link." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 604 222 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b4b6cd47-1f5d-5d8a-a3ff-8d9afb49ead6"))
  (text "The isolated half of each channel keeps 2.5 mm to every other net on every layer (ISO_IN class) and no pour of any net runs under it - see front-panel.kicad_dru and the two ISO keep-outs in the PCB." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 604 226 0) (effects (font (size 1.3 1.3)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a28fee60-e8fd-5061-8cae-0d5973ba17b5"))
  (text "J411 on the panel's LEFT EDGE: 1 = IN+, 2 = IN- (5-24 V DC, isolated, 5 kVrms). Wires enter off the edge." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 615 335 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e8b366ea-a25a-53fe-9b8e-508354c4a4bd"))
  (text "J412 on the panel's LEFT EDGE: 1 = IN+, 2 = IN- (5-24 V DC, isolated, 5 kVrms). Wires enter off the edge." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 615 490 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ac134ea8-5d1b-58fb-9199-5c2db053057e"))
  (text "SPARE SMA: shield on AGND, centre pin on TP1 only (no link pin)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 424 348 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "01c617ad-3ffd-5424-9978-26888208441b"))
  (text "The panel is passive: the rails come in through the link, so each one carries a power flag." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 60 396 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "bb1bc063-935a-559b-a17a-d5c9d7dc37d0"))
  (text "H1-H4: M3, same pattern as the main board (stand-offs). The OLED module's M2 holes are part of J30." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 200 398 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "5cf9b488-d087-5580-b395-924b8c3b9d01"))
